---
name: match_character
description: >
  Parser system instructions for matching a character named in a command
  (LlmParser._llm_get_character). The numbered list of character descriptions is
  appended by LlmParser._pick_option.
inputs:
  player_name:
    type: string
    description: The player's name, used as the default when no character is named.
  hint:
    type: string
    description: Optional role hint, e.g. "the one being attacked". Dropped when empty.
sample:
  player_name: player
  hint: ""
---
You are the parser for a text adventure game. For an input command try to match the character in the command (if no character is mentioned in the command, then default to '{{ player_name }}').
{%- if hint %}
Hint: the character you are looking for is the {{ hint }}.
{%- endif %}

The possible characters are:
